## 🎨 Design Patterns

### 1. Template Method Pattern
**Location:** Item.java

```java
public void printDetails() {
    // Common printing logic
    System.out.println("ID: " + itemId);
    // ...
    System.out.println(typeDetails()); // Abstract method
}
```

**Benefit:** Consistent output format with subclass customization

---

### 2. Strategy Pattern
**Location:** Tool.java, Appliance.java, Accessory.java

Each subclass provides different implementation of `typeDetails()`

**Benefit:** Different display strategies without modifying base class

---

### 3. Composite Pattern
**Location:** Item with associations

```java
private final List<Hobby> hobbies;
private final List<Equipment> equipment;
private final List<Facility> facilities;
```

**Benefit:** Uniform treatment of items with/without associations

---

### 4. Observer Pattern
**Location:** Logger.java

Observes all state changes across the system

**Benefit:** Centralized logging without tight coupling

---

### 5. Facade Pattern
**Location:** LibraryService.java

Provides simple interface to complex subsystem

**Benefit:** Reduces coupling, simplifies client code

